/-!
# Short recovery coverage for seeds 80–121

Each seed module checks all fifteen catalogues against the original short-case
selector and the literal compact generator walk. Exhausting this interval
therefore supplies the high-range premise of the full numeric coverage
assembly. Transition soundness converts these numeric witnesses into actual
seed members satisfying the original recovery equation.

Source: Parrott (1972), section 5, p.683; the literal Atlas normal forms and
`RecoveryChecks/source/README.md` with its two parent source READMEs.
-/

public section
namespace Tits.MinimumIndex.LargeTwoOvergroups.SeedOvergroups.ExtensionObstructions.RepresentativeCertificates.ShortCertificates.RecoveryAction

/-- Every literal short case in seeds 80–121 has a catalogue recovery walk. -/
theorem numericCoverageHigh : CoverageOn 80 42 := by
  intro i hlo hhi
  rcases i with ⟨i, hi⟩
  change 80 ≤ i at hlo
  change i < 122 at hhi
  interval_cases i
  · change Coverage 80 (stepData 80)
    exact coverage080
  · change Coverage 81 (stepData 81)
    exact coverage081
  · change Coverage 82 (stepData 82)
    exact coverage082
  · change Coverage 83 (stepData 83)
    exact coverage083
